logic	s5
atom	good_will	the will which makes use of these gifts is a good will
atom	gw_unqualified	a good will can be called good without qualification
atom	talents_unqualified	the talents of the mind and qualities of temperament can be called good without qualification
atom	fortune_unqualified	the gifts of fortune (power, riches, honour, health, happiness) can be called good without qualification
atom	talents_bad	the gifts of nature become extremely bad and mischievous
atom	fortune_pride	the gifts of fortune inspire pride and often presumption
atom	pleases_spectator	the sight of the prospering being gives pleasure to an impartial rational spectator
atom	worthy	the prospering being is worthy of happiness
# S1 read as: a good will is unqualifiedly good, and nothing else can possibly be.
P1	S1	gw_unqualified ∧ ¬◇talents_unqualified ∧ ¬◇fortune_unqualified	kind conceptual
